  1903	# _refresh_spec_contract — SPEC/v1 takes a FORCED route, NOT the generic
  1904	# backup_and_replace: for a directory target with a baseline, the classified
  1905	# walk PRESERVES adopter edits — so from the 2nd upgrade on, an edited SPEC
  1906	# would classify ADOPTER-CUSTOMIZED and the stale-contract class would
  1907	# return (r6). SPEC/v1 is the published compliance CONTRACT: an adopter edit
  1908	# is a FORK of the contract, not a customization (OQ-3) => backup to
  1909	# $BAK_DIR/SPEC/v1 + replace.
  1910	#   * ceremony: a recorded `--ceremony user` install NEVER receives SPEC/v1
  1911	#     (mirrors install.sh WS4-guard-spec), independent of --no-replay (r9).
  1912	#   * ownership: baseline SPEC records => framework-owned (forced refresh);
  1913	#     no target SPEC => new delivery; target SPEC with NO record => LEGACY
  1914	#     MIGRATION by pristine content (r20): match => framework-owned refresh,
  1915	#     no match => ADOPTER-FORK: preserve + snapshot + named WARNING.
  1916	#   * root VERSION: this function (and the whole upgrade) NEVER touches it —
  1917	#     install_one is skip-if-exists, so on an adopter with its own VERSION
