- P1 — Duplicate manifest records are marked invalid, but `_ov_obs_prior_record` ignores `_BASELINE_INVALID` and treats the retained first row as trusted ownership ([scripts/upgrade.sh:990](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.nPXKYg/wt/scripts/upgrade.sh:990), [scripts/upgrade.sh:1840](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.nPXKYg/wt/scripts/upgrade.sh:1840)). A duplicate `SPEC/v1/*` row therefore authorizes the forced delete-and-replace path at [scripts/upgrade.sh:2040](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.nPXKYg/wt/scripts/upgrade.sh:2040), violating fail-closed provenance handling.

- P1 — Downgrading with `--pin` to a pre-marker release drops marker ownership and claims the fallback `VERSION` reflects the pin ([scripts/upgrade.sh:2131](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.nPXKYg/wt/scripts/upgrade.sh:2131)). The same script explicitly never updates root `VERSION` ([scripts/upgrade.sh:346](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.nPXKYg/wt/scripts/upgrade.sh:346)), so a downgraded installation reports its stale install-time version, breaking update and forensic version state.

- P2 — An owned but emptied `SPEC/v1` loses ownership on an install rerun: continuity is asserted at [scripts/install.sh:2334](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.nPXKYg/wt/scripts/install.sh:2334), but the generator emits only files or symlinks and cannot serialize an empty directory ([scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:178](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.nPXKYg/wt/scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:178)). Subsequent upgrades misclassify the contract as an adopter fork and leave it empty.

The pure ownership oracle and shell syntax pass, but they do not cover these stateful provenance and pin transitions. The duplicate-record path can authorize replacement from explicitly ambiguous input, while the pin path deterministically publishes the wrong installed version; both make rc.2 unsafe to cut.

